\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  'Wake, awake! For night is flying',\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj The watchmen on the heights are crying.
\par 'Awake, Jerusalem, at last!'
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Midnight hears the welcome voices,
\par And at the thrilling cry rejoices:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj 'Come forth, you virgins, night is past!
\par The Bridegroom comes; awake,
\par Your lamps with gladness take, Alleluia!
\par And for his marriage feast prepare,
\par For you must go to meet him there.'
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Zion hears the watchmen singing,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj And all her heart with joy is springing;
\par She wakes, she rises from her gloom;
\par For the Lord comes down all-glorious,
\par The strong in grace, in truth victorious;
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj Her Star is risen, her Light is come!
\par Now come, O blessed One,
\par God's own beloved Son,
\par Alleluia!
\par We follow to the festal hall
\par \pard       To sup with you the Lord of all. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

